# Tierra Andina API — request examples.
# Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or JetBrains HTTP Client.
# Every error response has the shape { "error": { "code", "message", "details"? } }.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000

### Liveness — 200 { "ok": true, "version": "0.1.0" }
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Database check — 200 { "ok": true, "db": "up" } | 503 DB_UNAVAILABLE
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/db

### Unknown route — 404 NOT_FOUND
GET {{baseUrl}}/does-not-exist

### Unknown /api/v1 route — 404 NOT_FOUND
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/does-not-exist

# --- Auth (Better Auth). Browser requests carry Origin; foreign origins get 403 INVALID_ORIGIN.
# The REST Client keeps the session cookie between requests.

### Sign in — 200 + httpOnly session cookie | 401 INVALID_EMAIL_OR_PASSWORD
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/sign-in/email
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "owner@tierra-andina.local", "password": "change-me-dev-only" }

### Current user and stores — 200 | 401 UNAUTHENTICATED
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me
Origin: http://localhost:3000

### Owner briefing — week (Mon–Sun), deposited cash, open debts, fiados, alerts
# 200 for the owner. 403 for manager and receiver. There is no bank balance:
# `week.deposited` is cash marked deposited on this week's closes.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/home
Origin: http://localhost:3000

### Current session (Better Auth) — 200, body null when signed out
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/get-session

### Sign out — 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/sign-out
Origin: http://localhost:3000

### Sign up is disabled — 400 EMAIL_PASSWORD_SIGN_UP_DISABLED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/sign-up/email
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Nadie", "email": "nadie@test.local", "password": "password-123" }

# --- Products (docs/modules/products.md §5). Sign in first (request above).
# Reads: any role (receivers get only id, name, saleUnit). Writes: owner only.
# Errors: 404 PRODUCT_NOT_FOUND · 409 PRODUCT_NAME_TAKEN · 409 PRODUCT_UNITS_LOCKED ·
#         422 INVALID_UNIT_COMBINATION · 422 INVALID_PRODUCT_DEFAULTS · 422 CATEGORY_NOT_FOUND

### Categories — 200 { data: [{ id, code, name, sortOrder }] }
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/product-categories

### List — 200 { data, total, page, pageSize }; search ignores case and accents
### sort: name | category | updated, "-" prefix for descending (default name)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products?search=tomate&isActive=true&sort=-category&page=1&pageSize=20

### Create — 201 product (decimals as 4-decimal strings; lastMargin omitted → store default)
# @name createProduct
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Tomate perita",
  "categoryId": "<id of the 'vegetable' category>",
  "purchaseUnit": "crate",
  "saleUnit": "kg",
  "defaultPackQuantity": "24",
  "lastShrinkage": "2",
  "lastMargin": "0.5"
}

### Quick create (purchase screen) — 201; category "other", shrinkage 0, default margin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/quick
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Cilantro", "purchaseUnit": "bundle", "saleUnit": "unit", "defaultPackQuantity": "28" }

### Detail — 200 product + isUnitLocked
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/{{createProduct.response.body.id}}

### Update — 200; units rejected with 409 once the product is used
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/{{createProduct.response.body.id}}
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "lastMargin": "0.6" }

### Deactivate (soft delete) — 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/{{createProduct.response.body.id}}/deactivate
Origin: http://localhost:3000

### Activate — 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/{{createProduct.response.body.id}}/activate
Origin: http://localhost:3000

# --- Settings and daily rates
### Store settings — 200 { usdRoundingStep, bsRoundingStep, saleRateMode, saleRateMarkupPct, defaultMargin, receiverCanSeePrices }
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/settings

### Update settings (owner) — 200 all settings
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/settings
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "defaultMargin": "0.5" }

### Set the day's rates (owner): BCV (global), Coche (market) and sale — 200 { businessDate, bcv, market, sale }
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/exchange-rates/2026-10-19
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bcv": "200", "market": "201" }

### One day's rates (null when not set)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/exchange-rates/2026-10-19

### Days with rates in a range (≤ 62 days), newest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/exchange-rates?from=2026-10-01&to=2026-10-31

# --- Suppliers and purchases (owner). Errors: 404 TRIP_NOT_FOUND · 409 TRIP_CLOSED ·
#     422 DAY_RATES_MISSING · 404 LINE_NOT_FOUND · 422 LINE_PRODUCT_INVALID ·
#     422 SUPPLIER_NOT_FOUND · 422 INVALID_PURCHASE_LINE

### Suppliers — 200 { data }
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/suppliers

### Create a supplier — 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/suppliers
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Puesto de Juan", "stallReference": "Nave 3, puesto 7" }

### Open a trip — 201; copies the day's BCV and Coche rates (422 DAY_RATES_MISSING if not set)
# @name openTrip
# 409 TRIP_ALREADY_OPEN (details.tripId) while another trip of the store is still open.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/purchase-trips
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "businessDate": "2026-10-19", "note": "Lunes" }

### Trips — 200 { data, total, page, pageSize }
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/purchase-trips?status=open

### Add a line — 201 trip with lines. quotedPriceUsd is the line TOTAL in dollars.
### Omitted packs → crates not counted. Omitted shrinkage → the product's last shrinkage
### (the product is not changed). supplierRate defaults to the trip's Coche rate.
### Margin defaults to the product's last margin.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/purchase-trips/{{openTrip.response.body.id}}/lines
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": "<product id>",
  "stallReference": "Puesto 14",
  "packs": "3",
  "grossQuantity": "72",
  "shrinkage": "6",
  "quotedPriceUsd": "60",
  "paymentStatus": "paid"
}

### Trip with lines
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/purchase-trips/{{openTrip.response.body.id}}

### Truck receipt (owner or receiver) — 200 the trip as the receiver sees it (prices hidden
### for receivers unless receiverCanSeePrices). status: received | partial | missing | pending
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/purchase-trips/{{openTrip.response.body.id}}/lines/<line id>/receipt
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "partial", "receivedPacks": "2", "receivedQuantity": "47.5", "note": "Faltó una cesta" }

### Open trips with what to check at the truck — 200 { data: [{ id, businessDate, note, lines, toBuy }] }
### toBuy: open shopping-list items on the newest trip only (the receiver cannot call /shopping-list)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/receipts

### Close the trip — 200; lines can no longer change. Publishes the sale price list
### (422 SALE_RATE_MISSING if that day has no sale rate).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/purchase-trips/{{openTrip.response.body.id}}/close
Origin: http://localhost:3000

### What the shop still needs before Coche — 200 { data: [...] }, oldest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/shopping-list

### Add a missing product — 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/shopping-list
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": "<product uuid>", "note": "se acabó" }

### Drop an open request — 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/shopping-list/<item id>/drop
Origin: http://localhost:3000

### Sale prices in force (owner or manager) — 200, or 404 PRICE_LIST_NOT_FOUND
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/price-lists/current

### Sale-rate proposal (owner) — 200, or 404 PRICE_LIST_NOT_FOUND
# proposedSaleRate is null when today's rate is missing or moves no rounded Bs price.
# bcvChanged warns only; it does not reprice dollars.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/price-lists/proposal
Origin: http://localhost:3000

### Publish that proposal — 201 the new list (tripId null). 409 PRICE_PROPOSAL_UNCHANGED,
# 422 SALE_RATE_MISSING, 403 for a manager.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/price-lists/proposal
Origin: http://localhost:3000

### Daily close ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Amounts only, each in its own currency (no rate). Payment methods: GET /payment-methods
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/payment-methods

### Customers for credit sales (search by name)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers?search=mar

### Submit a close (manager or owner) — 201; 409 CLOSE_EXISTS if that day already has one.
### The manager can only send today; another day is 422 CLOSE_DATE_LOCKED (the owner may).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/daily-closes
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "businessDate": "2026-10-13",
  "cardBatch": "16",
  "cashDestination": "kept",
  "payments": [
    { "paymentMethodId": "<card_terminal id>", "amount": "163344" },
    { "paymentMethodId": "<cash_bs id>", "amount": "5500" },
    { "paymentMethodId": "<cash_usd id>", "amount": "18000" },
    { "paymentMethodId": "<mobile_payment id>", "amount": "83569" }
  ],
  "credits": [{ "customerName": "Sra. María", "amount": "1200", "currency": "VES" }],
  "expenses": [{ "concept": "Bolsas", "amount": "379", "currency": "USD" }]
}

### Closes of a range (newest first) with totals per currency
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/daily-closes?from=2026-10-12&to=2026-10-18

### One day
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/daily-closes/2026-10-13

### Waiting for the owner's review — 200 { count }
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/daily-closes/pending-count

### Correct (owner) — replaces payments, credit sales and expenses
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/daily-closes/<close id>
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "cardBatch": "16", "cashDestination": "deposited", "payments": [], "credits": [], "expenses": [] }

### Approve (owner) — 409 CLOSE_ALREADY_APPROVED the second time
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/daily-closes/<close id>/approve
Origin: http://localhost:3000

### Delete (owner) — 204. Approved closes too. That day can be submitted again. 403 for a manager
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/daily-closes/<close id>
Origin: http://localhost:3000

### Users of the active store (owner only), owners first; `isSelf` marks the caller
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users

### Create a manager or receiver with the password the owner gives — 201; 409 EMAIL_TAKEN
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "María", "email": "maria@tierra-andina.local", "password": "clave-inicial-1", "role": "manager" }

### Name, role or access — deactivating signs them out; 422 CANNOT_CHANGE_OWNER for an owner
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/<user id>
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "isActive": false }

### New password set by the owner — 204; the user is signed out everywhere
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/<user id>/password
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "password": "clave-nueva-2" }

### Tasks ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Active people a task can be assigned to (owner and manager)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tasks/assignees

### Tasks of the store: high priority first, then in progress, observation, pending, finished.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tasks

### Create a pending task (owner or manager) — 201; 422 ASSIGNEE_NOT_FOUND; 403 for a receiver
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tasks
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Comprar bolsas", "description": "Las grandes", "assigneeId": "<user id>" }

### Flag it, set the status (`pending`, `in_progress`, `observation`, `done`) or reassign it.
### A receiver may send only status — 403 otherwise
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tasks/<task id>
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "isHighPriority": true, "status": "in_progress", "assigneeId": "<user id>" }

### Delete (owner or manager) — 204. 403 for a receiver. 404 if it is already gone
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tasks/<task id>
Origin: http://localhost:3000

### Payables (owner; docs/modules/payables.md) ------------------------------------------------
### Supplier with its pago móvil accounts — 404 NOT_FOUND
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/suppliers/<supplier id>

### Edit a supplier — only the fields sent; "" clears a text
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/suppliers/<supplier id>
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "phone": "0414-5551234", "notes": "Trae el cambur los martes" }

### Add a pago móvil account — 201; stored as 04141234567 / V12345678. 400 for an unknown bank,
### a landline or a cédula without letter; 409 ACCOUNT_EXISTS (same bank and phone)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/suppliers/<supplier id>/accounts
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bankCode": "0102", "phone": "0414-123.45.67", "idDocument": "V-12.345.678" }

### Replace an account's data (PUT) or deactivate it (DELETE) — 404 ACCOUNT_NOT_FOUND
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/suppliers/<supplier id>/accounts/<account id>
Origin: http://localhost:3000

### Expense categories for supply lines
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/expense-categories

### Invoices, newest first; status = pending | partial | paid | overdue | voided (derived).
### `balance` adds up what the filtered invoices owe, per currency
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/payables?status=overdue&supplierId=<supplier id>&page=1&pageSize=20

### A supplies invoice — 201 with code CXP-000123. Currency USD (default) or VES.
### 422 SUPPLIER_NOT_FOUND · 422 EXPENSE_CATEGORY_NOT_FOUND (details.fieldErrors)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/payables
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "supplierId": "<supplier id>",
  "currency": "USD",
  "issuedOn": "2026-10-18",
  "dueOn": "2026-10-25",
  "lines": [
    { "description": "Bolsas medianas", "expenseCategoryId": "<category id>", "quantity": "10", "unit": "pack", "unitPrice": "1.50" }
  ]
}

### One invoice with lines and payments — 404 PAYABLE_NOT_FOUND
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/payables/<payable id>

### Replace a supplies invoice (same body as POST) — 409 PAYABLE_HAS_PAYMENTS,
### 409 PAYABLE_FROM_PURCHASE (merchandise: correct the purchase), 409 PAYABLE_VOIDED
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/payables/<payable id>
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "supplierId": "<supplier id>", "issuedOn": "2026-10-18", "dueOn": "2026-10-25", "lines": [] }

### Due date and note (any invoice not voided) — 422 INVALID_DUE_DATE before the issue date
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/payables/<payable id>/terms
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "dueOn": "2026-10-30", "note": "Paga el viernes" }

### Void (no payments) — 409 PAYABLE_HAS_PAYMENTS, 409 PAYABLE_VOIDED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/payables/<payable id>/void
Origin: http://localhost:3000

### A payment — 201. method: mobile_payment | bank_transfer | cash_bs (Bs) | cash_usd (divisa).
### rate = BCV of the payment day. 422 PAYMENT_EXCEEDS_BALANCE (details.balance in the
### payment's currency) · 422 INVALID_PAYMENT_ACCOUNT · 409 PAYABLE_VOIDED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/payables/<payable id>/payments
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "paidOn": "2026-10-18", "method": "mobile_payment", "amount": "5000", "rate": "201.5", "reference": "001234", "accountId": "<account id>" }

### Delete a mistaken payment — 200 the invoice; 404 PAYMENT_NOT_FOUND
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/payables/<payable id>/payments/<payment id>
Origin: http://localhost:3000

### What to pay today by pago móvil: balance in Bs (USD at today's BCV) and the "Pegar datos"
### text per active account. 422 BCV_RATE_MISSING · 409 PAYABLE_SETTLED · 409 PAYABLE_VOIDED
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/payables/<payable id>/mobile-payment
